#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Shows Spatial Audio (status, the default), or turns it on, off or over (toggle). While it is on, songs with Spatial Audio play as their Spatial Audio rendition where Apple allows it, and in stereo otherwise. It applies from the next song."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Shows crossfade (status, the default), or turns it on, off or over (toggle). Its length stays as set in Settings → Playback."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Shows private listening (status, the default), or turns it on, off or over (toggle). While it is on, nothing you play is reported to Apple, scrobbled or kept in Sona's history."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Shows repeat (status, the default), or sets it: off, all (the queue) or one (the playing song). cycle moves on as the player bar's repeat button does: off, all, one, off."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Shows shuffle (status, the default), or turns it on, off or over (toggle), as the player bar's shuffle button does."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Shows the commands, or one command's arguments and options. With --man it prints the manual page in roff instead."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Shows the playback state, the song, its position, the volume, shuffle, repeat, crossfade and private listening. With --follow it keeps running and prints one line each time any of them changes (the position alone doesn't count), for status bars such as Waybar and Polybar; it ends when Sona quits. When Sona isn't running, it says so and exits with status 3."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Shows whether the playing song is in your library (status, the default), adds it (add), removes it (remove) or switches it (toggle). `library playlists` and `library albums` list your library's playlists and albums, most recently added first, with the links `sona play` takes. Needs an Apple Music account signed in to Sona."
msgstr ""

