#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "With --json, a command prints one JSON object on standard output; `status --follow --json` and `lyrics --follow --json` print one per line. Fields are only ever added, never renamed or removed. Errors go to standard error as text, with the exit status below."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Without a link, resumes playback, or starts the queue Sona saved when it last quit. With an Apple Music link to a song, album, playlist or station (your library's included, as `sona library playlists` lists them), plays it in place of the queue; --shuffle starts the album or playlist shuffled. Prints the status line."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "Without a value, shows the volume. A number from 0 to 100 sets it; +N or -N changes it by N."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "`sona addons dev <folder>` runs the add-on in a folder without installing it and prints its log until you press Ctrl+C. Sona asks you to confirm in its window, naming the folder and the permissions its manifest asks for; nothing is saved and the permissions end with the run. The add-on's ID can't be one you have installed, it gets none of your saved secrets, and the folder must be yours and not writable by others. A native add-on needs Linux for now; a WebAssembly add-on (\"runtime\": \"wasm\") runs on every system."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "`sona` starts Sona, or brings the running one to the front. Apple Music links among the arguments open in it. --hidden starts it without a window (playback, media keys and the tray only), as the start-at-login entry does. --version prints the version."
msgstr ""

#: internal/cli/messages.go
msgid "`status --format TEMPLATE` prints each status through a Go text/template whose fields are the JSON fields (`{{.state}}`, `{{with .track}}{{.artist}} – {{.title}}{{end}}`, `{{.volume}}`); `{{json .x}}` quotes a value as JSON and `{{clock .position}}` writes seconds as m:ss. With --follow it suits Waybar's and Polybar's custom modules. `lyrics --follow` takes the same options for the line being sung (`{{.text}}`)."
msgstr ""

